{%- comment -%}
  LEGACY WORDPRESS URL SAFETY NET
  ---------------------------------
  Catches old morghew.com /shop/* URLs that should redirect but currently 404
  in Shopify's own redirect engine, despite correct records existing in
  Settings > URL Redirects. This is a STOPGAP, not a replacement: keep the
  real Admin redirects in place (most fire correctly) and escalate any that
  still 404 after this to Shopify Support - a true 301 is stronger for SEO
  than this page-level catch. Once a path's real redirect is confirmed
  working (test with curl -I), delete both its lines below (with and
  without the trailing slash).

  IMPORTANT - why this matches in JavaScript, not Liquid: inside the 404
  template's render context, {{ request.path }} is always "/404" - Shopify
  does not expose the originally-requested URL to Liquid here. The real URL
  only exists client-side as window.location.pathname. An earlier version of
  this file compared against request.path and therefore could never fire,
  on any path, regardless of how correct the target list was - it silently
  did nothing. Do not "simplify" this back to a Liquid comparison.

  2026-08-27: rebuilt on that basis, and the path list was trimmed from the
  original 168 entries down to 68, keeping ONLY targets confirmed live on
  the storefront (verified by curl against every target on the launch
  catalogue). The other 100 old WP URLs point at products that were not
  carried into the new store's ~48-SKU launch range (hampers, hay/straw,
  sweet potatoes, wild game selections, seasonal mixes, decorative lines,
  etc) - redirecting those would have bounced visitors from one dead page
  straight into another. See George/Craig for whether any of those should
  be re-added (pointing at a live substitute or a collection page) once
  decided.

  TO ADD A PATH NOT ALREADY LISTED: add TWO entries to legacy_pairs - one
  without a trailing slash, one with - format from-path>to-path,
  comma-separated. Case-sensitive exact match. Verify the target resolves
  (not a 404) before adding it - don't reintroduce a broken redirect.
{%- endcomment -%}

